%% Kiro-API V3 — request lifecycle (one chat turn)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client (harness)
    participant R as Route shim (OpenAI/Anthropic/ACP)
    participant S as ShimService
    participant A as AuthManager
    participant P as WorkerPool
    participant W as ACP worker (kiro-cli acp)

    C->>R: POST /v1/chat/completions (or /v1/messages, /acp/chat)
    R->>S: normalized messages + model + MCP servers
    S->>A: auth gate (logged in?)
    alt not logged in
        A-->>S: LOGGED_OUT
        S-->>C: 401 authentication_error (native shape)
    else logged in
        S->>P: lease(worker, timeout)
        alt pool saturated + queue full
            P-->>S: OVERLOADED
            S-->>C: 503 / 429 + Retry-After
        else worker leased
            P-->>S: worker
            S->>W: session/new (cwd, mcpServers) → session/prompt
            loop streaming events (idle-timeout bounded)
                W-->>S: text / thinking / tool_call / plan
                S-->>C: SSE delta (+ keepalive when idle)
            end
            W-->>S: done (stopReason)
            S-->>C: final chunk + [DONE]
            P->>P: return worker to idle (or retire if dead)
        end
    end
